  "id": "COMPOUND:26385 - PROTEIN:1106",
  "verbalization": "Boseongazepine C appears to exert its biological effects through a shared target, Proto-oncogene tyrosine-protein kinase Src, which is targeted by multiple compounds, including Boseongazepine C, Eschweilenol C, and 2-Phenylpropan-1-Ol. These compounds all lead to the activation of the Gamma-aminobutyric acid receptor subunit gamma-2, suggesting a common mechanism of action involving Src. The evidence is supported by high scores in the final_score metric, indicating a strong and consistent relationship across different pathways. The mechanism likely involves Src-mediated signaling pathways that influence the function of the GABA receptor subunit gamma-2, potentially through modulation of receptor activity or downstream signaling cascades. The presence of multiple independent pathways converging on the same target reinforces the likelihood of a mechanistic link, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact nature of the interaction.",
